<details class="flow-basics" id="flow-basics"><summary>Automation flow guide</summary><section id="flow-guide-start"><h2>Build your first flow</h2><ol><li>Choose a template or build from scratch. Creating a flow saves a draft.</li><li>Choose a starting point, such as confirmed signup or adding a tag, and any entry filters.</li><li>Add your emails and audience actions. Review every branch and its exit.</li><li>Save the draft, then review it before choosing to turn it on.</li></ol><a href="<?= $h($url(['view'=>'flow-templates','preview'=>'welcome'])) ?>">Explore the welcome template →</a></section><section id="flow-guide-logic"><h2>Starting points, conditions and timing</h2><p>Any of a flow’s starting triggers can add a qualifying connection. If/Else conditions choose one path using current audience data. Delays wait for a duration; trigger waits choose a matching or timed-out path. Repeat settings and entry/exit filters apply separately.</p><p>Existing connections do not enter just because you created a draft. New qualifying activity after activation starts the flow; authorized manual entry still respects its filters and repeat rules.</p></section><section id="flow-guide-delivery"><h2>Review before turning on a flow</h2><p>Every email needs its sender, subject and content. Email steps require a currently subscribed connection and qualified delivery; unsubscribe, archive and removal checks continue to apply. Drafts and checklist progress never enable sending.</p><p>Pausing a flow keeps connections in place. Activated revisions preserve the email and map used by connections already in progress. Restoring a removed flow creates a draft.</p></section></details>
